.DS_Store

# The Go rewrite. Two entries, both for the same reason: a compiled artefact is not
# source and `go build ./...` will make one in every directory that has a `main`.
/darkroom
/darkroomdb
# `bin/` holds TRACKED scripts (`bin/prime`, `bin/tier-counts`), so it cannot be
# ignored wholesale — and `/darkroom` above is root-anchored, so it does not cover
# the binary `go build -o bin/darkroom ./cmd/darkroom` writes, which the gate's own
# build step performs. That combination is how a 21 MB artefact gets committed by a
# `git add -A` during verification.
/bin/darkroom
*.test
*.out
